[orch:err] ### milvus-io/milvus#51393 — feat: nested element-level indexes for plain scalar arrays
[orch:err] - State: `OPEN` · Closing-link from PR: no · Source: `cross`
[orch:err] - URL: https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/pull/51393
[orch:err] - Author: xiaofan-luan
[orch:err] - Labels: kind/feature, sig/testing, size/XXL, approved, area/test, area/internal-api, dco-passed, test/integration
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] #### Issue body
[orch:err] issue: #46517
[orch:err] design doc: `docs/design-docs/design_docs/20260620-scalar-array-element-match-design.md` §5/§7 (+ `.zh.md`)
[orch:err] > **Stacked on #50669** (#51385 layer 6 — the stack top for the feature). Review the last commit. ⚠️ This PR carries the entire rolling-upgrade surface, deliberately isolated.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## What
[orch:err] Plain-ARRAY scalar indexes (BITMAP/INVERTED/sort family incl. HYBRID/AUTOINDEX) build as NESTED element-level indexes (value → element-id postings) once the cluster's resolved scalar index engine version reaches 5, accelerating MATCH_*/element_filter through the same element-level lookup struct sub-field indexes already use.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] - **Marker, not version inference**: legacy row-level and nested shapes coexist, distinguished ONLY by a per-segment `is_nested_index` marker. The rule (`typeutil.IsNestedArrayIndex`: plain ARRAY + not struct sub-field + version ≥ 5) is enforced at THREE independent decision sites — datacoord build request, **index worker re-derivation** (an old datacoord that resolves v5 from upgraded querynodes still yields a nested build), and snapshot/copy re-derivation — so no version-skewed peer can break the invariant. Missing/false → legacy loader + brute-force MATCH. On-file flags win over the marker on disagreement (mis-marked index degrades loudly or correctly, never silently).
[orch:err] - **Array equality via the index**: `arr == [..]` / `!=` served by positional AND over element bitsets (row length == k ∧ element at position i matches v_i) with 3VL NULL exclusion — removes the brute-force regression for existing equality workloads after an index rebuilds nested. Other whole-array ops keep the RawData fallback.
[orch:err] - Memory-estimate floors (BITMAP + sort mmap, marker-gated), element-level cache skips, `nested_index` reserved as a user param, Avro manifest v5, restore guard refusing nested onto pre-v5 pools.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## Review guide
[orch:err] - **The review anchor is the design doc's upgrade/rollback matrix (§7.2)** — try to construct a version pairing that breaks "v5 plain-ARRAY ⟺ nested". The three decision sites: `internal/datacoord/task_index.go` (isNestedArrayIndex), `internal/datanode/index/task_index.go` (normalizeNestedIndexMarker), `internal/datacoord/copy_segment_task.go` (syncVectorScalarIndexes).
[orch:err] - Known, documented limitation: **rollback below v5 after nested indexes exist is NOT detected** (old binary drops the proto field) — operational rule: reindex or restore first.
[orch:err] - Tests: per-family nested build/load/all-null/mmap round-trips, indexed-vs-brute differentials (incl. equality: duplicates, order sensitivity, prefix rows, empty target, NULL rows under NotEqual), marker meta round-trip + legacy defaults, copy-path re-derivation (dropped echo restored / bogus echo cleared / unresolvable-field fallback), restore version guard, estimate-floor differentials. 834/834 C++ + datacoord/datanode Go at this layer.
[orch:err] 
[orch:err] ## Release note
[orch:err] New plain-array index builds are element-level once all querynodes run v5. Do not downgrade querynodes below v5 after nested indexes exist. Whole-array non-equality comparisons on nested indexes execute brute-force.
[orch:err] 
